<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hōjō Ujinao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1562–1591</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Hojo Ujinao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hōjō Ujinao was the fifth and last head of the Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-clan">Hojo clan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawara">Odawara</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. With his father Ujimasa he refused to submit to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, who besieged Odawara in 1590. After the surrender Ujimasa was ordered to kill himself, but Ujinao, son-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>, was spared and exiled to Mount Koya, where he died the next year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hojo-ujinao.jpg" alt="Hōjō Ujinao" width="320" height="512" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hojo_Ujinao.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
